\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Opens Higher Against Dlr, Stays Steady \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1996\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened higher against the U.S. dollar Tuesday and weakened slightly in the course of quiet morning dealing. \par \par \uc2  Around 0920 GMT Tuesday, the dollar was at 2.7052 zlotys, up slightly from 2.7045 zlotys at the opening and down from Monday's fixing of 2.7120 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.8235, unchanged from the opening and up from Monday's fixing of 1.8195 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty was following dollar-mark trends on international markets, and so was stronger against the dollar and weaker against the mark. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the dollar was trading at 1.4842 marks, down from 1.4856 marks late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the National Bank of Poland set the parity rate at 2.7548 zlotys on the dollar and 1.8582 zlotys on the mark. The zloty is allowed to float within a band of plus or minus 7 points around the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at about 1.8% below its parity rate on Tuesday. The mark was about 1.9% below its central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  In the past, the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the dollar from falling below 2.5% of the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  But now, foreign investors have taken the place of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dampening zloty appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Investors sell Polish Treasury bills and buy dollars for zlotys when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls to about 2.3% below the parity rate, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money-market rates were indicated at between 16.30% and 17.20%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-07-96 \par \par \uc2  0938GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds7n060d1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
