\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty -2: Foreign Investors Seen Buying T-Bills \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 1996\par 10:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that Polish banks were betting that foreign investors who had pulled out of the market for Polish Treasury bills during the Russian election campaign would return now that Yeltsin's victory over communist challenger Gennady Zyuganov in Wednesday's balloting is almost certain. \par \par \uc2  In the course of the morning, the dollar briefly dipped below the level of 2.7000 zlotys, to 2.7180 zlotys, as Polish banks sold the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for zlotys. But 'There was fairly strong support for the dollar at that level,' said Bogdan Stepkowski of ING Bank, and it recovered somewhat. \par \par \uc2  The zloty 'could strengthen further in the course of the day,' said one dealer at a Western bank. \par \par \uc2  However, this dealer said he feared that Western investors might now move more of their funds into Russia and pull out of investments in Central Europe. \par \par \uc2  But Mateusz Bienek of Societe Generale said the zloty should continue to strengthen now that the cloud of the Russian elections has been removed. \par \par \uc2  The dollar on Thursday slipped to about 1.9% below the parity rate established by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The mark was trading at close to 2% below its central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Bienek said the dollar could eventually weaken further, to the level of 2.5% below the parity rate. That is the level at which the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'It seems to me it will test the level of 2.5% in the long term,' Bienek said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 19.70% and 20.35%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-07-96 \par \par \uc2  0847GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds7405hzh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
