\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Weakens Slightly Vs Dollar, Stabilizes \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1996\par 11:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty dipped slightly against the dollar but then stabilized in calm dealing Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0915 GMT, the dollar was at 2.7120 zlotys, up from 2.7090 zlotys at the opening and from Monday's fixing of 2.7115 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7680 zlotys, down from 1.7703 zlotys at the opening but up from Monday's fixing of 1.7650 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  'The market is very calm, very stable,' said Malgorzata Sawicka at Bank Handlowy. 'Volume is very low. There was a small wave of dollar buying at first,' which later dissipated, she said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at about 1.9% below the central parity rate, a level that is tolerated by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has generally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls below 2.5% of the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Sawicka said the mark's weakness against the zloty was a reflection of its dip against the dollar on international markets. \par \par \uc2  The dollar and mark have the greatest weight in the basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to which the zloty is pegged. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 21.45% and 21.53%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-06-96 \par \par \uc2  0944GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds6b04tcy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
