\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Slips Against Dollar And Deutsche Mark \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 1996\par 10:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened higher but then slipped against the dollar in quiet pre-weekend dealing on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the dollar was at 2.6912 zlotys, up from 2.6893 zlotys at the opening but down from Thursday's fixing of 2.6930 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7465 zlotys, up from 1.7450 zlotys at the opening and from Thursday's fixing of 1.7430 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The zloty was trading at about 2.48% above the central parity rate for the dollar. Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely at that level. \par \par \uc2  Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday drove the zloty down to within about 2.5% of its parity rate to the dollar, from 3% earlier that day. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers continued to attribute the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to political factors. \par \par \uc2  They noted that the National Bank of Poland has been under pressure from politicians to damp the appreciation of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to boost flagging Polish exports. \par \par \uc2  In an interview on Radio Zet Friday morning, National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz declared: 'We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in a way that is pro-export.' \par \par \uc2  She said other factors were to blame for the problems of Polish exporters. Among them is the country's 48% payroll tax to fund the social security program, which adds to company costs and reduces Poland's wage competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 21.50% and 21.54%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-05-96 \par \par \uc2  0848GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds5o04aob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
