\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Gains Ground Ahead Of Treasury Bill Sale \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1996\par 11:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened lower against the dollar on Monday but gained in the expectation that foreign investors would be buying Treasury bills at the afternoon auction. \par \par \uc2  Around 0920 GMT, the dollar was at 2.6725 zlotys, down from 2.6745 zlotys at the opening but higher than Friday's fixing of 2.6680 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7398 zlotys, down from 1.7413 zlotys at the opening and from Friday's fixing of 1.7430 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's strong opening against the zloty reflected its rise against the mark in international markets. \par \par \uc2  But in dealing on Monday, the zloty started gaining ground against both the dollar and the mark. The trend bore no relation to events on international markets, said Tomasz Wlad of Amerbank. \par \par \uc2  Rather, he said, dealers were bidding up the zloty in anticipation of the T-bill auction. 'There's light pressure for the sale of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' Wlad said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  was calling banks to check quotations but had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown that it will tolerate a deviation from the central parity rate of 2.8%,' said Jacek Baprawski of Bank Polska Kasa Opieki SA. \par \par \uc2  That was about the level at which the zloty was quoted against the dollar and mark on Monday. Dealers said the chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  therefore seemed fairly strong. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 21.40% and 21.60%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-05-96 \par \par \uc2  0951GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds5k046da\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
