\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Opens Down Against Dollar, Up Versus DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1996\par 12:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was slightly lower against the collar in calm dealing on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 1025 GMT, the dollar was at 2.6275 zlotys, up from 2.6255 zlotys at the opening and from Tuesday's fixing of 2.6235 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar reached a peak of about 2.6283 before retreating slightly, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7415 zlotys, down from 1.7500 zlotys at the opening but up from Tuesday's fixing of 1.7400 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Mateusz Bienek of Societe Generale said the zloty was tracking movements in the dollar-mark on international markets. \par \par \uc2  The dollar and mark have the biggest weighting in the basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to which the zloty is pegged. \par \par \uc2  'The market is calm,' Bienek said. 'We don't expect any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be holding back, given that widely-expected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday failed to materialize. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.55% and 22.75%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-04-96 \par \par \uc2  1052GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds4h0391p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
