\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Opens Lower Vs Dollar, Inches Upward \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 1996\par 12:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened lower against the dollar but inched upward in the course of the morning on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0930 GMT, the dollar was at 2.6153 zlotys, down slightly from 2.6165 zlotys at the opening but up from Wednesday's fixing of 2.6135 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7405 zlotys, down from 1.7425 zlotys at the opening and from Wednesday's fixing of 1.7430 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The zloty's rise against the mark was a reflection of the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness against the dollar on international markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the zloty was showing some strength against the dollar as a result of increased interest in Polish Treasury bills by foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  Polish dealers said the interest in T-bills resulted from an improved rating issued Wednesday by Standard & Poor's. \par \par \uc2  The agency said it had raised its rating on Poland's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated debt to triple-B-minus from double-B. \par \par \uc2  Standard & Poor's also assigned its A-1 rating to Poland's short-term zloty-denominated debt. \par \par \uc2  Upward pressure on the zloty aroused concerns about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been checking the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The market is thin, and spreads are wide because banks don't want to be caught off guard,' said a dealer at Societe Generale in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.65% and 22.75%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-04-96 \par \par \uc2  1006GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds4b033k7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
