\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Opens Lower Against Dollar, Inches Up \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1996\par 10:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened more than 1 grosz lower against the dollar but inched up in the course of the morning on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the dollar was at 2.6125 zlotys, down from 2.6155 zlotys at the opening but up from Tuesday's fixing of 2.6040 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7435 zlotys, up from 1.7415 zlotys at the opening but down from Tuesday's fixing of 1.7460 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  With the dollar and mark trading at an average of about 2.6% below their central parity rates, dealers said they didn't expect a repetition of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'There isn't much interest in the sale of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Bogdan Stepkowski of ING Bank. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy marks for zlotys at the level of 1.7480 zlotys when the Germany \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to about 2.8% below its central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Marcin Trzygowski, a dealer at Bank Polska Kasa Opieki SA, said he expected the dollar to remain above the level of 2.6100 zlotys. 'That level could be tested, but I doubt it will fall lower,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's upward move against the zloty was a reflection of its strength against the mark on international markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates on Wednesday were indicated at between 22.65% and 22.73%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-04-96 \par \par \uc2  0852GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds4