\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Dips Vs Dlr After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Edges Up \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 11:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty dipped against the dollar following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday but then continued to edge upward, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar moved up violently' after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one dealer said. 'The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't very large but it had a big psychological effect.' \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland bought dollars at the level of 2.5845 zlotys, dealers said. At that level, the dollar was trading at 2.9% below its central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move, the dollar briefly rose to a high of 2.5935 zlotys before slipping again, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0955 GMT, the dollar was up to 2.5913 zlotys, compared with 2.5840 zlotys at the opening and Wednesday's fixing of 2.5810 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7435 zlotys, down from 1.7400 zlotys at the opening and from Wednesday's fixing of 1.7390 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had apparently abandoned its previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of 2.5% below the parity rate for the dollar and was now defending a new level of 2.9% below parity. \par \par \uc2  Andrzej Rzysko, treasurer at Societe Generale in Warsaw, welcomed the apparent change in policy, saying it represented a relaxation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's grip on Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  'I was really surprised that the National Bank of Poland was keeping at the 2.5% level for such a long period,' Rzysko said. \par \par \uc2  A change in policy, he said, 'would give dealers greater scope to trade.' \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.65% and 22.81%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1020GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3s02ra1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
