\par\par \b \uc2  ZLOTY GAINS AS MARKET BAFFLED BY NO NBP ACTION. \b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, March 26 (Reuter) - The zloty rose against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid the dollar/mark's sideways drift in Europe as the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defied expectations and did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the bullish zloty, leaving dealers baffled. \par \par \uc2  The zloty has been rising against both the dollar and the mark throughout the day fuelled by some $110 million of accepted foreign bids at Monday's primary T-bill tender. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty when the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed above 2.5 percent from the parity rate -- the centre of the daily 14-percent trading band. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the NBP although actively checking rates, bought no \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market and let the zloty rise to 2.69 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates. \par \par \uc2  "The market expected a NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  all day taking the zloty higher with each quoting and waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reaction," said Jerzy Wyjadlowski of Bank Slaski SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 2.5785/00 to the dollar, up from yesterday's 2.5800/07 and at 1.7458/65 to the German mark, also up from 1.7483/89 yesterday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said no NBP reaction to the zloty's rise today meant the market would probe yet higher tomorrow. \par \par \uc2  "Tomorrow banks will try to take the zloty higher because they want to know where the new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level is," said Tomasz Nowakowski of Bank Handlowy SA. "Maybe the NBP will let the zloty rise to three percent from the parity rate," he said. \par \par \uc2  But other dealers said the NBP was only playing a game with the market because it wanted to pay less zlotys for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  flowing into Polish T-bills and would re-establish its old \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels when the client orders are over tomorrow. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt if the NBP had let the zloty go. It seems more like a one-day phenomenon to absorb \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  more cheaply," said Bogdan Stepkowski of ING bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the secondary T-bill market was quiet with some deals done of the benchmark 52-week paper at 21.05 percent -- down from the average yield of 21.10 percent at the last primary tender on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The NBP sold its 182-day paper at an unchanged average yield of 22.20 percent but rejected all bids for its 91-day bills, which last sold at 21.96 percent. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates eased 0.02 point to 22.70/22.80 percent, and tromorrow/next rates 0.05 point to 22.75/22.80 percent despite a 180 million 14-day drainage with a maximum rate 0.02 point up at 22.89 percent.-- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040127ds3q005q0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
