\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  Zloty Down Slightly After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 12:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was down slightly against the dollar and Deutsche mark Monday following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying of both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 1125 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5805 zlotys, compared wilth 2.5780 zlotys at the opening and from Friday's fixing of 2.5820 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7495 zlotys, compared with 1.7485 at the opening and Friday's fixing of 1.7460 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars at the level of 2.5790 zlotys and 2.5795 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought marks at the level of 1.7492 zlotys and 1.7490 zlotys, dealers said. The scale of buying of both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were small, with transactions limited to about $5 million each, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'It was just a show of presence' by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Andrzej Rzysko, treasurer at Societe Generale in Warsaw. 'The price hasn't reacted very strongly to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started buying when the average departure from parity rate for the dollar and mark dipped to minus 2.55%, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bogdan Stepkowski of ING Bank said the demand for zlotys was spurred by foreign investors putting in bids for treasury bills at the weekly auction scheduled for Monday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.75% and 22.84%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1120GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3p02lzz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
