\par\par \b \uc2  Polish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  steps in to stop zloty rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, March 20 (Reuter) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty just before the market closed Wednesday, reaffirming it had no intention of letting the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen in the near term, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to show that it would not let the zloty rise in the near term," said Mateusz Bieniek of Societe Generale. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported a clear dollar selling trend in the market today on possible renewed foreign buying of Polish T-bills amid growing expectations of an interest rate cut. \par \par \uc2  "The market sentiment has long been in favour of the zloty but today it could have been augmented by some foreign entry into Polish T-bills," said Bieniek. \par \par \uc2  To stop the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been creeping up against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since opening, the NBP bought an estimated $30 million on the market through a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranging from 2.5741 zlotys through 2.5748 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  started when the zloty moved up to 2.56 percent from weighted dollar and mark parity rate -- the centre of the daily 14-percent trading band -- and was brought back to a previous NBP-establised level of 2.53 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said renewed foreign interest in Polish paper, although not large, was likely to have been influenced by better-than-expected February inflation data which spurred expectations of a near-term interest rate cut. \par \par \uc2  Inflation last month was 1.5 percent against the expected 1.8 percent and January's 3.4 percent, which took the year-on-year index down to 20.4 percent from 21.2 in January. \par \par \uc2  "There is no big rush from foreigners yet, but we might see more of them at the next primary T-bill auction on Monday because February inlation data spurred rate cut expectations," said Piotr Bednarek of ING bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expected the NBP could cut its discount and lombard rates, now at 23 and 26 percent respectively by about one point in response to the consumer price data. \par \par \uc2  "I expect a one point interest rate cut very soon as the NBP promised to have smaller but more frequent rate moves in line with falling inflation," said Barbara Kowalczyk, analyst at Bank Gdanski SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Poland's current account data, which showed a surplus if cross-border inflows were taken into consideration, would keep the zloty testing the NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels for weeks to come. \par \par \uc2  "Cash flow data shows demand for the zloty is rising and banks will keep testing NBP levels in the weeks, eventually forcing the zloty up -- maybe to three percent from parity," said Jan Mieczkowski, treasurer at Deutsche Bank here. \par \par \uc2  However, some dealers said the NBP could keep the zloty at 2.5 percent from the parity rate until the third quarter of this year. \par \par \uc2  -- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds3k0a68n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
