\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Opens Lower Against Dollar, Then Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par 12:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened lower against the dollar but rose slightly in the course of the morning on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 1050 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5334 zlotys, down from 2.5350 zlotys at the opening but up from Monday's fixing of 2.5220 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7423 zlotys, up from 1.7415 zlotys at the opening but down from Monday's fixing of 1.7475 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar and mark together were trading at about 2.5% below their parity rates. That is generally considered the level below which the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty was tracking movements in the dollar-mark on international markets, meaning that the level of the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  together should not deviate much more from their parity rates. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, one dealer said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible. \par \par \uc2  'The National Bank has been calling and checking prices,' the dealer said. 'If the dollar falls much more, there could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.20% and 22.45%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-02-96 \par \par \uc2  1110GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2k01i65\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
