\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty closes firmer vs dlr, eyes Buba, depos up. \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 14 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty closed stronger against the dollar and softer to the mark in line with world trends, keeping clear of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels and quietly trailing dollar/mark changes, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's estimated $100 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty yesterday showed the NBP was determined to keep it at current levels about 2.55 percent from the central parity rate -- the centre of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  "The market was very quiet after yesterday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reacted mainly to the small changes in the dollar/mark rate," said Marek Golebiewski of PBK SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty's short-term moves could hinge on tomorrow's Bundesbank council meeting because the NBP already clearly establised the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ceiling and there were no new domestic factors. \par \par \uc2  "Trade tomorrow is likley to be focused on the Bundesbank's fortnighly council meeting," said Zbigniew Choszcz, chief dealer at Bank Gdanski SA. The zloty closed at 2.5428/35 to the dollar, up from yesterday's 2.5472/82 and at 1.7297/01 to the mark, down from 1.7253/55. \par \par \uc2  One-day rates rose 0.2 point to 22.40/22.55 percent as recent reverse repos and NBP-bill auctions drained the market. \par \par \uc2  The secondary T-bill market was quiet as few players were offering the most sought longer-term paper. The 26-week and 39-week bills were traded at 21.10/20.80 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very quiet and lives from one primary T-bill tender to another," said Krzysztof Czarkowski of BRE SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were pleasantly surprised by the higher yield at the NBP's 91-day paper auction today saying it could be a signal yields might be bottoming out after a six week slide. \par \par \uc2  "The higher 91-day yield today was a nice surprise which might be a signal yields could be bottoming out," Czarkowski said.   -- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2e01gyq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
