\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Inches Up Vs Dlr; Slips Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 1996\par 12:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty continued to inch up against the dollar on Wednesday, tracking the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements against the Deutsche mark on international markets. \par \par \uc2  Around 1110 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5425 zlotys, down from the opening of 2.5442 and from Tuesday's fixing of 2.5480 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The mark was at 1.7303 zlotys, up from 1.7295 zlotys at the opening and from Tuesday's fixing of 1.7260 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was little chance of a repetition of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'Everyone has sold their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Wojciech Trzepizur of Bank Inicjatyw Gospodarczych BIG S.A. \par \par \uc2  The average departure from the parity rate for the dollar and mark on Wednesday was within the bounds tolerated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purchases of dollars and marks appeared to set a new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of 2.55% below the average parity rate for the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Previously, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to be triggered when the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below 2.50% of their average parity rates. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.30% and 22.50%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-