\par\par \b \uc2  NBP  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  shackle foreign-charged zloty. \b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 13 (Reuter) - The zloty, propelled upward by large-scale foreign entry in Poland's T-bill tender on Monday, repeatedly attacked \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, only to be forced back by the bank's mark and dollar purchases. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated that today's National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  drained between $80 and $100 million from the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and clearly established the 2.55 percent from parity as the zloty's near-term resistance. \par \par \uc2  "Strong foreign entry in Monday's auction created a huge supply of dollars on the market, which was in turn drained by numerous NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Marek Szarlej of PBKS SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 2.5472/82 to the dollar, down from yesterday's 2.5452/58, this loss reflecting the dollar's rise against the mark, and at 1.7253/55 to the mark, up from 1.7260/65. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 2.5455, 2.5460 and 2.5480 zlotys and marks between 1.7255 and 1.7265 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty's charge could ease on Wednesday, the settlement date for the T-bills, but that the sentiment was bound to return and keep the NBP defending resistance levels. \par \par \uc2  "Pressure is sure to be on the NBP, but judging by recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bank intends to keep the zloty close to 2.5 percent from parity," said Andrzej Kopec of Bank Slaski SA. \par \par \uc2  The parity rate is the centre of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 14-percent trading band, set daily by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  using the value of a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a devaluation factor. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said T-bill yields continued to drop on the secondary market, with 52-week T-bills, sold on Monday with an average yield of 20.76 percent, trading today at 20.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  However, the amount of offers on the market increased from last week, which some dealers said could be a sign that yields were starting to bottom out. \par \par \uc2  "More offers on the market could mean the market is slowly starting to balance out," said Pawel Wolczynski of ING bank. \par \par \uc2  "However, dropping yields at today's NBP-bill sale show the market is hungry for paper even at lower yields," he said. \par \par \uc2  The average yield for 182-day NBP-bills was 21.30 percent, down from 21.47 percent for a comparable 26-week T-bill at Monday's auction, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the average yield of its 91-day paper at 21.35 percent, just down from 21.39 percent for a comparable 13-week T-bill from the last auction. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates closed flat at 22.30/22.40 percent, while tomorrow/next rates rose 0.05 point at bid to 22.35/22.50. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2d01iqk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
