\par\par \b \uc2  Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 /Dollars -2: Buys At 2.5455 Zlotys \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1996\par 12:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying dollars and Deutsche marks for zlotys. \par \par \uc2  At around 1120 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars twice at the level of 2.5455 zlotys and 2.5460 zlotys, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought marks three times, at 1.7260 zlotys, 1.7261 zlotys and 1.7263 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The average departure from the central parity rates for both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty was minus 2.53%, said a dealer at ING Bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , noting that an earlier round of dollar and mark purchases on Tuesday morning had failed to halt the slide of those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty. \par \par \uc2  'There's a big supply of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market right now, said Piotr Konarski of Bank Handlowy. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  routinely declines to confirm or deny \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Around 1100 GMT, shortly before the latest round of buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was quoted at 2.5452 zlotys, up from 2.5445 zlotys at the opening but down from Monday's fixing of 2.5460 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7256 zlotys, down from 1.7280 zlotys at the opening and from Monday's fixing of 1.7270 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-02-96 \par \par \uc2  1148GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2d01b1r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
