\par\par \b \uc2  NBP stops zloty rise vs dlr, mark, depo rates flat. \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 5 (Reuter) - The bullish Polish zloty managed to close firmer against the dollar even though it was stopped in its stride by several \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and might again test higher ground tomorrow, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the zloty's advance today was likely to be fuelled by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows from payments for digital mobile phone system (GSM) licences totalling $260 million, foreign investment in Polish T-bills and on the Warsaw bourse. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling trend could be connected to payments for the GSM licences among other inflows," said Przemyslaw Ciszecki of ING bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which came at 2.5400 and 2.5410 zlotys against the dollar and at 1.7205 against the mark at a total of about $60 million. \par \par \uc2  "The market shows strong inclination to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and we are likely to see the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels tested again in the near-term," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The NBP has been stepping in against the zloty whenever the Polish unit rose above 2.5 percent from the central parity rate -- the centre of the 14-percent trading band. The zloty closed at 2.5390/00 to the dollar, up from Friday's 2.5495/05 and at 1.7210/25 to the German mark, down from 1.7140/50 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  One-day rates were flat at 22.60/22.70 percent throughout the day, signalling that the money market found its balance at that level after last week's swings. \par \par \uc2  Trade on the secondary T-bill market was stiffled by the primary auction which drew 2.5 billion zlotys worth of bids for a 600 million zloty offer. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All average yields fell, with the benchmark easing 0.2 point to 22.59 percent despite expectations that it would stabilise.\tab  -- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (c) Reuters Limited 1996\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds250381f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
