\par\par \b \uc2  Polish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to block zloty rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 5 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the domestic interbank market to keep the zloty down despite upward pressure from banks with surplus dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the banks' foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales were probably fuelled by the remains of inflows from last week's tobacco firm sales and GSM licence payments. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland bought marks at 1.7205 and dollars at 2.5410 zlotys as the zloty broke resistance at 2.5 percent from the central parity rate -- the centre of a 14 percent trading band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the zloty moved above 2.5 percent from the parity rate, signalling it did not want a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimated at a total of about $30 million, came when the zloty firmed to 2.58 percent from the parity against the dollar and 2.52 percent against the mark. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the zloty was quoted at 2.5400/10 against the dollar and 1.7201/11 against the mark. \par \par \uc2  Last Wednesday, the NBP bought more than $100 million on the market in a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to 2.61 percent from the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was sparked by a client order to sell the bulk of $130 million that Germany's Reemtsma paid for the Poznan tobacco firm. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the $227 million which Philip Morris paid for the Krakow-based cigarette factory on Tuesday was sold mostly at the post-trade fixing. But some said small amounts of dollars from the Reemtsma deal remained to be sold after Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also said Monday's sales could have been fuelled by part of $260 million which two Polish-dominated consortia had to pay to the government for digital mobile phone network licences (GSM) awarded last week. \par \par \uc2  Under the agreement with the government the consortia have two weeks to pay for the licences. \par \par \uc2  -- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds25037x8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
