\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Up Slightly Vs Dlr in Slow Dealing \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1996\par 12:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-DJ)--The Polish zloty was up slightly against the dollar in quiet dealing on Friday, with banks holding back for fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 1020 GMT, the dollar was at 2.5515 zlotys, down from 2.5530 zlotys at the opening but up from Thursday's fixing of 2.5495 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7141 zlotys, virtually unchanged from 1.7140 zlotys at the opening and from Thursday's fixing of 1.7140 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said banks were quoting narrow spreads and keeping to within 2.5% above the parity rate for the dollar and mark to fend off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  After \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, 'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  demonstrated that it's going to strongly defend the level of 2.5%,' said Bogdan Stepkowski of ING Bank. \par \par \uc2  In addition, he said, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  consistently sets the afternoon fixing rate at a maximum level of 2.5% above the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  As a result, banks hesitate to go above that level during the day's trading because they may not be able to close their positions at the fixing without taking a loss. \par \par \uc2  Marek Kucharski of Bank Gospodarki Zywnosciowej said there was practically no speculative trading on Friday. 'It's all client orders,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers predicted that recently announced foreign investments in Poland's tobacco industry, as well as the flow of foreign money into the booming Warsaw Stock Exchange, would lead to continued upward pressure on the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.55% and 22.70%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-02-96 \par \par \uc2  1106GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds220113v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
