\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Down Against Dollar in Calm Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1996\par 11:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-DJ)--The Polish zloty was lower against the dollar on Friday in calm trading. \par \par \uc2  Around 1050 GMT, the dollar was at 2.4868 zlotys, up from 2.4850 zlotys in the morning but down slightly from Thursday's fixing of 2.4870 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7195 zlotys, unchanged from the morning and up from Thursday's fixing of 1.7165 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar and mark were within 2.5% of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity rates for those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meaning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, dealers predicted selling pressure on the dollar was likely to continue, and that banks would probably test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's informal barrier. \par \par \uc2  'There's big pressure to sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' which occurred early in the week, said Jaroslaw Kubiak of Powszechny Bank Kredytowy. \par \par \uc2  But Pawel Gajewski of Creditanstalt said that 'the banks are holding back' for the time being, and that trading would be guided by the action on international markets. \par \par \uc2  'Now, only movement on the dollar-mark can change something,' Gajewski said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 24.90% and 25.30%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-01-96 \par \par \uc2  1010GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds150066o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\pics