\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Lower Vs Dollar As Market Stabilizes \b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 1996\par 12:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-DJ)--The Polish zloty was lower against the dollar Thursday, as the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained against the Deutsche mark in international markets. \par \par \uc2  Around 1110 GMT, the dollar was at 2.4852 zlotys, up from 2.4830 zlotys in the morning and from Wednesday's fixing of 2.4755 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7181 zlotys, virtually unchanged from 1.7180 zlotys in the morning but down from Wednesday's fixing of 1.7215 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  'There is little chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Bogdan Stepkowski of ING Bank in Warsaw. 'The market is resting.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily Tuesday and Wednesday to keep the dollar and mark within 2.6% of their parity rates against the zloty. \par \par \uc2  The heavy selling pressure was caused largely by foreign investors seeking to buy Polish Treasury bills on the expectation of a further appreciation of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, with the Polish market stable, dealers once again turned their attention to movements in the dollar-mark on international markets. They found little guidance, with the dollar range-bound against the mark. \par \par \uc2  As a result, 'The (Polish) market is trying to decide what to do next,' said Robert Wysocki, senior dealer at Polski Bank Inwestycyjny. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated between 25.00% and 25.25%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-01-96 \par \par \u