\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Will Continue To Rise, Analysts Predict \b0\par\par\uc2  By CHRISTOPHER WELLISZ \par \uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1995\par 17:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-DJ)--The Polish zloty will continue to rise against the dollar and Deutsche mark following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to lower the central parity rates for those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said Friday. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the zloty's rise against the dollar was limited to 2.4% following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP). But analysts say the market will continue to test what appears to be a new limit set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'The upward pressure will continue,' said Maciej Krzak, an economist at ING Bank in Warsaw. 'We will see a market-driven appreciation of the zloty whenever the NBP will allow for it.' \par \par \uc2  Late on Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a 6% cut in the parity rates for the dollar and mark. The parity rate for the dollar was lowered to 2.5360 zlotys from 2.6988 zlotys. The rate for the Deutsche mark also was lowered 6%, to 1.7610 zlotys from 1.8735 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  By the close of trading on Friday, the dollar sank to 2.4750 zlotys, down from Thursday's fixing of 2.5360 zlotys. The Deutsche mark closed at 1.7140 zlotys, down from Thursday's fixing of 1.7610 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The zloty would have made further gains against the dollar and mark but for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. 'The bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilized the market,' said Bogdan Stepkowski, a dealer at ING Bank. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-12-95 \par \par \uc2  1642GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drcm0a9ar\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
