\par\par \b \uc2  Poland Zloty Opens Lower Against Dlr, Holds Steady \b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 1995\par 12:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-DJ)--The Polish zloty opened slightly lower against the dollar on Thursday but held steady in the course of the morning. \par \par \uc2  Around 1130 GMT, the dollar was at 2.4665 zlotys, little changed from the opening of 2.4660 zlotys but up from Wednesday's fixing of 2.4610 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7535 zlotys, up from 1.7525 zlotys at the opening but down from Wednesday's fixing of 1.7565 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  'The market is neutral,' said Bogdan Stepkowski, a dealer at ING Bank's Warsaw branch. 'It's following the course of the dollar-mark.' \par \par \uc2  With both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 6% and 6.1% below the parity rate set by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said there was little chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In Europe around 1055 GMT, the dollar was at 1.4062 marks, compared with 1.4068 marks both in Tokyo around 0530 GMT and late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Polish overnight money market rates were indicated at between 25.55% and 25.65%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1158GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drbg08zf1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
