\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Up Slightly Against Dlr, Steady on DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1995\par 12:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-DJ)--The Polish zloty is up slightly against the dollar and steady against the Deutsche mark on Friday amid signs of continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 1100 GMT, the dollar was at 2.4605 zlotys, down slightly from the opening of 2.4620 zlotys in the morning and from Thursday's fixing price of 2.4710 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was unchanged at 1.7445 zlotys on Friday and up slightly from Thursday's fixing of 1.7360 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the dollar at about 2.4600 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  'The bank showed it doesn't want the dollar to fall below 6.15% from the parity rate,' the dealer said. The morning's parity rate for the dollar was set at 2.6213 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The decline of the dollar against the zloty was a reflection of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness against the mark, said Bogdan Stepkowski of ING Bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Around 1110 GMT in Europe, the dollar was quoted at 1.4095 marks, down from 1.4132 marks around 0530 GMT in Tokyo and steady from 1.4095 marks late Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  In Poland, overnight money market rates for the zloty were indicated at 25.40% to 25.55%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-11-95 \par \par \uc2  1156GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drba08uld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
