\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty extends dlr gains,mark losses,trade balanced. \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Oct 23 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty firmed slightly against the dollar and lost more ground against the mark as spreads narrowed in early balanced trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said expectations of a potential western \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar against the mark put domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling on hold and was likely to keep the zloty closely trailing dollar/mark moves during the day. \par \par \uc2  "The market is eyeing the dollar/mark rate, wary of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which would boost the dollar and the zloty is likely to stay tuned to world trends today," said Zbigniew Choszcz chief dealer at Bank Gdanski SA. \par \par \uc2  At 0910 the zloty was quoted at 2.4300/15 against the dollar, up from 2.4295/35 at the opening and 2.4435/55 on Friday. It was at 1.7480/00 against the mark, down from 1.7455/75 at opening and 1.7340/55 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market unless the zloty firmed to 6.1 percent from the floating central parity rate -- the value of the zlotys against a basket of western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At 0913 GMT the zloty/dollar rate was 6.05 percent from the floating parity. \par \par \uc2  "The NBP is likely to leave the market alone until the 6.1 percent level is reached," said Bogdan Stepkowski of ING bank. \par \par \uc2  On the money market overnight and tomorrow next rates eased 0.05 point to 25.55/25.60 percent on a 260 million zloty net inflow today and a 512 million zloty inflow tomorrow. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also said the market was more liquid because tax payments in some banks would not come until tomorrow. \par \par \uc2  "The market seems more liquid and trade is balanced," said Marta Tabor of Pekao SA. The secondary T-bill market was moribund ahead of today's 850 million primary auction. "Secondary trade thrives mainly on clients, and they prefer to buy at primary auctions because of better yields," said Rafal Chodzidlo of Bank Slaski SA.-- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dran02opz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
