\par\par \b \uc2  Polish mkts to probe new NBP  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  levels. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jan Strupczewski \par \uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Aug 11 (Reuter) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relaxed approach to zloty rate swings this week is likely to keep the market guessing next week just how lenient the NBP's rate policy might have become, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The NBP, usually stepping in with dollar and mark purchases when the zloty firmed to five percent from the daily parity rate, let the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise to 5.1 percent against the mark on Thursday before it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop it. \par \par \uc2  The bank did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars this week even though interbank offers often hovered at 5.08 percent from the dollar central parity. \par \par \uc2  "The NBP seemed to cut the zloty more slack this week, though it is not clear just how much more freedom it will get," said Marcin Szereda of Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Even the zloty's rise to 1.6920/30 against the mark today, or 5.13 percent from the parity rate, failed to prompt any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said however, the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the usual "five percent" level was just a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruse to make the potential \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchase levels less predictable. \par \par \uc2  "The NBP still wants to keep the zloty at the 'five percent' but is getting involved at slightly different levels to confuse the market and make the timing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  less obvious," said Maciej Wegrzynski, treasurer at ING bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said daily \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues from exports, tourism and unregistered cross-border trade exerted strong upward pressure on the zloty, and were likely to keep it probing higher against the dollar and the mark next week. \par \par \uc2  But they also said the rise of the zloty was doomed to meet \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resistance sooner rather than later because of an exports protection deal between the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said the ministry agreed to the partial flotation of the zloty in May, in exchange for a promise the NBP would not allow the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to firm more than five percent from the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The zloty strenghtened three percent after the flotation, but analysts said it would have gained more were it not for the NBP's firm stand. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8b053ic\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
