\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty closes weaker vs dollar despite small gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Aug 8 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty failed to regain ground lost against the dollar overnight despite small intraday gains but was seen making another attempt at the upside tomorrow, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said today's clear dollar-selling trend combined with a lack of National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the usual five percent from parity rate level could inspire banks to push the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher tomorrow. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty's potential gains today were hampered by confusion as to how the NBP would react -- at which level it would step in with an intrevention" one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The NBP usually started buying dollars or marks when the zloty firmed to five percent above the daily parity rate. \par \par \uc2  But today, for the third day in a row, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not only allowed the zloty to trade lightly above the "five percent" level during the day, but also fixed the zloty at 5.04 percent above dollar parity and 5.02 percent above the mark parity. \par \par \uc2  "This signals a change in the NBP's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market policy," said Piotr Konarski of Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  "It is likely that the NBP will now defend the five percent level, but not from the central parity rate as until recently, but from the floating parity rate," he said. \par \par \uc2  The floating parity is based on the value of a basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and follows rate movements on world markets. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market the zloty closed at 2.3990/00 against the dollar, down from 2.3880/95 yesterday and 1.7015/25 against the mark, up from 1.7050/65. The NBP declined comment but some analysts hinted the bank was ready to become more flexible about the "five percent" level in order to keep the value of the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  unchanged. \par \par \uc2  On the money market one-day rates edged higher on a net outflow of 385 million zlotys in reverse repo payments and after the NBP's Open Market Committee (KKOOR) announced it had left its repo rate flat at 26.5 percent until August 21. \par \par \uc2  In the afternoon overnight and tomorrow/next rates rose 0.05 point to 26.6/26.65 and 26.6/26.7 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  "It is likely that banks waited for the KKOOR announcement holding back with purchases in case the repo rate was cut and started searching for cash only after the announcement was published close to midday," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  -- Jan Strupczewski +48 2 625 6303 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8805898\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
