\par\par \b \uc2  POLISH ZLOTY CONSOLIDATES VS DOLLAR. \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 19 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty clung onto its overnight gains against the dollar despite the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's small rise against the mark, signalling an underlying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling mood, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But they said the summer trade slow-down and apprehension of possible National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were likely to keep the zloty subdued tomorrow. \par \par \uc2  "A weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling sentiment was there, but fear of the NBP's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the zloty goes too high and the holiday season make any spectacular moves unlikely," said Piotr Konarski of Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that in the absence of fresh fundamental factors the zloty was likely to stay in a band from 4.8 to 4.9 percent from the NBP's central parity rate tomorrow. \par \par \uc2  Some traders pointed out however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not step in today when the zloty briefly firmed to 2.3670 against the dollar or 4.92 percent from parity, which might signal it was easing its grip on the market. \par \par \uc2  "It seems that after knocking it down with a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  two weeks ago, the NBP is now cutting the zloty more slack," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 2.3670/75 against the dollar, up from 2.3720/37 yesterday and at 1.7070/80 against the mark, down from 1.7032/54. \par \par \uc2  On the money market one-day rates eased slightly in late afternoon trade because today's 883 million zlotys \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drainage would be fully offset by tomorrow's reverse repo inflows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates were down 0.05 point at bid at 26.45/26.60 percent while tomorrow/next rates fell 0.05 point at offer to 26.3/26.55 percent. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the 172 million zloty two-year and five-year bond auction tomorrow was likely to see bids mostly for the longer-term papers. \par \par \uc2  They said that considering year-on-year inflaiton still run above 30 percent in June the satisfactory yield for the five-year bonds was around 23 percent. \par \par \uc2  Traders said a satisfactory yield for the two-year bonds would be at about 25 percent -- a level which the treasury was unlikely to accept. \par \par \uc2  -- Jan Strupczewski +48 2 625 6303 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040126dr7j004rr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
