\par\par \b \uc2  Polish Nat bank buys marks to stop zloty rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 5 (Reuter) - Polish zloty inched up against the mark and eased to the dollar in light trade, following international trends, during a light trading day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market selling zloties, as the Polish unit drifted high from the zloty/mark parity rate, the centre of the 14-percent daily trading band. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty made gradual gains on the mark as it eased against the dollar (on world markets), and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped further potential gains of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Andrzej Kepa, chief dealer at BDK SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 1.6932/51 to the mark, flat from this morning and up from  1.6962/72 yesterday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought marks at 1.6945 and 1.6947 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The zloty eased from opening against the dollar to close at 2.3458/67, after Tuesday's close of 2.3425/30. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates rose 0.15 points at bid to 26.65/26.75 percent, as banks paid for Monday's 327 million zloty T-bill auction. Tomorrow/next rates held flat at 26.45/26.75. \par \par \uc2  "Cash was expensive, O/N bids topped the one-day drainage rate of 26.5 percent, and few banks were active," said Daniel Posyniak of ING bank.  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 2 625 6303 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr7506322\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
