\par\par \b \uc2  Polish zloty breaks NBP resistance vs mark. \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, June 28 (Reuter) - The zloty firmed against the mark, breaking through the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, as the German unit lost a half a pfennig against the dollar on world markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In speculative trade, the zloty strengthened to about 5.35 percent away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity rate, the mid-point of the daily 14-percent trading range, shattering old \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels of near 5.15 from parity. \par \par \uc2  "Many banks build long mark positions during the day in hopes of sell them, at a handsome profit, at the NBP's fixing," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that today's mark fix, at 5.17 percent from parity and well below the market rate, was, in effect, another form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying of the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 1.6881/93 to the mark, up from 1.6911/34 at opening, and yesterday's close of 1.6920/30. It closed at 2.3460/70 to the dollar, easing from 2.3420/30. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the NBP's tactics were in a sharp contrast to yesterday, when the bank frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the trading day, virtually freezing market rates and fixing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at closing market levels. \par \par \uc2  Most traders said today's approach gave the market more freedom to steer the exhchange but some said the frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were better because they offered stability. \par \par \uc2  Money market rates continued to be offered above the NBP's one day drainage rates of 26.5 percent, as some banks were making last minute efforts to beef up required monthly reserve levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the market's liquidity improved and tomorrow/next rates closed down 0.25 points at bid, flat at offer at 26.35/26.8, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 571 million zloty drainage. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 2 625 6303 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr6s06ckf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
