\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central bank interventions \highlight\uc2  freeze Polish zloty. \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, June 27 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily on the domestic interbank market on Tuesday to stop the zloty's surge, casting doubts over the market's freedom to drive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland floated the zloty domestically last month by broadening the daily trading range from four to 14 percent around a central parity rate. The rate is set each day by the bank on the basis of pre-announced crawling devaluation and cross rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least three times on Tuesday as the zloty strengthened above the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level at 5.16 percent from parity. \par \par \uc2  After opening at 2.3425/55, five percent below parity, the zloty had no room to strengthen when the dollar started loosing ground to the mark internationally. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said because the parity rate is set once a day before the market opens, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stiff adherence to the five percent limit does not account for rate changes during the trading day. \par \par \uc2  "The parity rate becomes obsolete whenever the dollar makes significant moves internationally...and has little in common with the zloty's actual market value," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  After the market was liberalised last month, bankers long on dollars due to booming exports, pushed the zloty about five percent above the parity rate, easing some pressure on money supply. \par \par \uc2  But then as they tried to push the zloty further, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in selling zlotys whenever the zloty/dollar rate fell more than five percent from parity. \par \par \uc2  "The 14-percent trading range is only theoretical. The practical range is between five and 5.2 percent below parity," said Marcin Stefaniuk, dealer at BDK bank. \par \par \uc2  "It's a one way market, the zloty hits a brick wall at the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level almost every day, and no matter what happens with the dollar and the mark (on world markets), the zloty simply cannot firm more," said Jacek Baprawski of PKO SA. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said that they are pleased with the current market level at five percent from parity because a further appreciation could harm exports. \par \par \uc2  They expect imports to pick up in the next few months, causing hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows which would naturally depress the zloty and limit \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would free the zloty from the five percent band, the market would find its real balance only a half a point lower. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr6r06bzp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
