\par\par \b \uc2  ZLOTY SEEN BRAVING  \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK INTERVENTION \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jan Strupczewski \par \uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, June 12 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty is likely to test new highs against the dollar this week despite expected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buoyed by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows from official and unregistered exports, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market with dollar and mark purchases to slow down the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's climb after it was partially floated on the domestic interbank market on May 16. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have usually come when the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened against the dollar or mark by more than five percent from the central parity rate -- the mid-point of a 14-percent trading band, calculated on the basis of a basket of five western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a monthly devaluation factor. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said however that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level at five percent below parity was untenable in view of the dollar's weakness on world markets and mounting dollar-selling pressure from exports revenues. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be forced to shift the 'five percent' level lower down (this) week because of the pile-up of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from exports and cross-border trade in banks," said Zbigniew Chmielewski, deputy treasurer at ING bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  "It is likely to do so because its intention does not seem to be to reverse the zloty climb but only to slow it down, in which it succeded," he said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty ended the latest week at 2.3425/45 against the dollar, virtually flat compared with 2.3420/50 the Friday a week ago even though the dollar fell by almost one pfennig against the mark to about 1.40 during that period. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the zloty's potential gains were capped by a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity rate to 2.3701 on Friday to the dollar today from 2.4614 a week earlier, which moved the five-percent below parity \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level higher. \par \par \uc2  "The market wants to sell dollars but fear of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the zloty down," said Artur Pilewicz of PKO BP bank. "There is almost no speculation because the risks are too high in case of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and banks deal mainly on clients' orders," he said. \par \par \uc2  On the money market dealers expected one-day zloty deposit rates to stay in the 25.5-26.5 percent range this week, pegged to the new one-day repo rate of 26.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to stage several open market drainages to help absorb the high liquidity of the market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures show banks will receive a net inflow of some 2.62 billion zlotys next week. \par \par \uc2  "One-day rates are likely to stay in the 25.5-26.5 percent range with a bias towards the lower end because of the excess liquidity of the market," said Jaroslaw Maczkowski of BDK SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that after several recent outright T-bill sales at which the NBP accepted higher yields than the finance ministry at its primary auction, the market was now likely to focus on today's 1.1 billion zloty primary T-bill tender. \par \par \uc2  They said banks are likely to bid for higher yields at today's auction expecting to place cash at an NBP outright if their bids are rejected. \par \par \uc2  "If the ministry plays it tough and keeps yields down, the NBP is likely to stage an outright sale to absorb the cash surplus not drained at the primary auction," said BDK's Maczkowski. \par \par \uc2  At the last outright sale the yield accepted by the NBP was about 0.3 point higher than that accepted by the treasury on a bill of comparable maturity at the primary auction. \par \par \uc2  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 625 6303 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130dr6c006lk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
