\par\par \b \uc2  Polish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to halt zloty rise. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Adam Jasser \par \uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 23 (Reuter) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, halting the zloty's rapid appreciation against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  For the first time since it floated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the domestic market last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold zlotys to banks at 2.3675 to the dollar after the Polish unit had soared by more than one percent in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The zloty briefly rose further to reach 2.3600, before the market became fully aware of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped back. \par \par \uc2  "In our opinion, this appreciation was a little too fast and we wanted to give a signal to exporters, worried about the possibility of a major rise of the zloty," NBP's deputy president Krzysztof Barburski said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave domestic traders a taste of new hazards on the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, brought by the flotation. \par \par \uc2  "We have what we wanted, a market run by supply and demand but one full of risks if you stick your neck out too far," said Marek Chrobak of Bank Zachodni SA. \par \par \uc2  Last Tuesday the NBP allowed banks to trade the zloty within a band of seven percent above and below a special parity rate. The rate is set each morning on the basis of world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crosses and taking into account the monthly devaluation of the zloty against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Previously the zloty was confined to a four percent band and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the market tone each day by quoting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the commercial banks did. The flotation gave the zloty, undervalued due to high foreign trade inflows, room for appreciation and allowed market forces greater influence on the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Bankers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate up to three percent after the move and the NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday set the rate exactly at that level. \par \par \uc2  Economists have long advocated a zloty revaluation, either by floating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or through an administrative one-off appreciation, saying this was the only way to ease monetary pressure caused by swelling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chose the former, believing it would guarantee a gradual appreciation that would be less harmful to Poland's booming exports. \par \par \uc2  Following the float, the zloty was appreciating slowly but this week the trend accelerated and Tuesday's zloty gains moved it five percent away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity rate of 2.4830, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Our role is to stabilise the trend and not to allow large volatility," central banker Barburski said. "In my opinion the market was speculative today." \par \par \uc2  Following the NBP action rates stabilised at around 2.3670 to the dollar and bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level had become a resistance point for the zloty. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr5n07jgd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
