\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's NBP  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  to serve monetary goals. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Adam Jasser \par \uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, May 14 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be guided by long-term monetary goals and the state of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the domestic market after a partial float of the zloty, the bank's deputy head said on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Krzysztof Barburski told a meeting of bankers that floating of the zloty on the domestic market on May 16 would shift the main role in setting the exchange rate from the National Bank of Poland to commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  "The shaping of the rates will principally depend on you," he said at an annual conference of Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers. \par \par \uc2  "Our main guidance will be long-term monetary policy targets and the second important factor will be the state of reserves." \par \par \uc2  Under the new rules, domestic banks will be free to set exchange rates within a 14 percent band around the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mid-rate. \par \par \uc2  The rate will be set each morning on the basis of world market rates and will also take into account the preannounced monthly devaluation of the zloty, now at 1.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  Up to now the band was only four percent and the banks were able to deal with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only at this band's top and bottom limits. This gave the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the dominant role in setting the exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  Now, Barburski said, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to send rates in a desired direction. \par \par \uc2  It will also hold an early afternoon auction, during which it will make a fixing, based on the bids and offers from banks willing to square positions with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Barburski said this method would allow fixing to reflect more closely market rates. \par \par \uc2  "The fixing should be close to the average between the interbank market's bid and offer rates," he said. \par \par \uc2  The fixing, announced at about 1500 local time, would serve as a reference for all transactions with non-banking clients. \par \par \uc2  Barburski said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in such a way as to make its policy predictable by market players. \par \par \uc2  "You will be making decisions about rates but we want you to be able to understand our policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said the market could be very volatile initially but should gradually settle down once the new rules are digested. \par \par \uc2  He also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would aim at guiding the market rather than pushing the rates in a desired way. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decided on a partial float of the zloty in the hope that it would allow the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate, stemming the rapid growth of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  They also say the move would make monetary policy more flexible and the exchange rate more in tune with market condidions. \par \par \uc2  Bankers estimate that the zloty, which closed on Friday at 2.46 to the dollar, could appreciate by up to three percent after the float, but they also say the size of the appreciation will be chiefly determined by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  One banker said that shortly after the flotation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to impose, through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the desired level of appreciation, only later leaving it to the market to set the rate. \par \par \uc2  "I think the bank will make a policy decision about the scope of the zloty appreciation because this is why these new regulations were introduced in the first place," the banker said. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 625 6303 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr5e07u5w\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (poland near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri